/* Ad057 - Memory leak / unbounded RSS after STEPCAFControl_Reader
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   Catalog section : §12.11 adversarial (sub-class: resource-exhaustion)
   Sources         : 18-other-issues.md I017 (ShapeFix_Shape huge memory),
                     I018 (Linux/Docker RSS),
                     I019 (LSAN reports STEPControl_Controller::Init enum
                           allocations leaked)
   See also        : Ad027
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   WARNING: This file is INTENTIONALLY MALFORMED for parser-robustness
   testing. Do NOT use as exchange data.
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   Defect
     After read of a moderate STEP file, RSS does not return to baseline
     (e.g. ~900 MB held after a 142 MB file on glibc); ShapeFix on huge
     shells hangs and consumes huge memory. LSAN reports leaks from
     STEPControl_Controller::Init enum tables that are never freed.
   Reproducer recipe
     File with many enum-typed slots that flood the typed-value tables
     (here: many BOOLEAN/LOGICAL slots), exercising leak in the
     enum-table allocator.
   Expected kernel behavior
     Bypass/chunk shell-fix at large counts; release working set on
     destruction; free typed-value tables on shutdown.
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------
*/
